Solve the following equation algebraically for \(\theta\), where \(0 \leq \theta \leq 2 \pi\) :
\[
2 \cos 2 \theta=1
\]

\section*{Solution}

Method 1
\[
\begin{aligned}
2\left(2 \cos ^{2} \theta-1\right) & =1 \\
4 \cos ^{2} \theta-2 & =1 \\
\cos ^{2} \theta & =\frac{3}{4} \\
\cos \theta & = \pm \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \\
\cos \theta & =-\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \\
\frac{1 \pi}{6} \quad \theta & =\frac{5 \pi}{6}, \frac{7 \pi}{6}
\end{aligned}
\]

