Prove the identity for all permissible values of \(\theta\) :
\[
\cos \theta+\tan \theta \sin \theta=\frac{\tan \theta \sin \theta}{1-\cos ^{2} \theta}
\]

\section*{Solution}

\begin{tabular}[t]{|l|l|}
\hline Left-Hand Side & Right-Hand Side \\
\hline \[
\begin{aligned}
& \cos \theta+\tan \theta \sin \theta \\
& \cos \theta+\frac{\sin \theta}{\cos \theta} \sin \theta \\
& \cos \theta+\frac{\sin ^{2} \theta}{\cos \theta} \\
& \frac{\cos ^{2} \theta+\sin ^{2} \theta}{\cos \theta} \\
& \frac{1}{\cos \theta}
\end{aligned}
\] & \[
\begin{aligned}
& \frac{\tan \theta \sin \theta}{1-\cos ^{2} \theta} \\
& \frac{\frac{\sin \theta}{\cos \theta} \cdot \sin \theta}{\sin ^{2} \theta} \\
& \frac{\sin ^{2} \theta}{\cos \theta} \cdot \frac{1}{\sin ^{2} \theta} \\
& \frac{1}{\cos \theta}
\end{aligned}
\] \\
\hline
\end{tabular}

