![](https://cdn.mathpix.com/cropped/d40a5513-7bb4-48ff-98e6-c9f731122cdf-31.jpg?height=541&width=587&top_left_y=612&top_left_x=221)
\[
\begin{aligned}
\cot \theta & =\frac{x}{y} \\
r^{2} & =x^{2}+y^{2} \\
r^{2} & =(-1)^{2}+(3)^{2} \\
r^{2} & =10 \\
r & = \pm \sqrt{10} \\
\sin \theta & =\frac{3}{\sqrt{10}}
\end{aligned}
\]
\(\frac{1}{2}\) mark for substitution
\(\frac{1}{2}\) mark for solving for \(r\)
1 mark for \(\sin \theta\) ( \(\frac{1}{2}\) mark for the quadrant, \(\frac{1}{2}\) mark for the value)
2 marks

Note(s):
\begin{itemize}
\item[-] accept any of the following values for \(r: r= \pm \sqrt{10}, r=\sqrt{10}\)
\end{itemize}

