Given the following characteristics of a sinusoidal function:
\begin{itemize}
\item[-] an amplitude of 2
\item[-] a vertical translation down 3 units
\item[-] a period of \(\frac{\pi}{4}\)
\item[a)] Determine an equation of this sinusoidal function in the form \(y=a \sin b(x-c)+d\).
\item[b)] Determine the range of this function.
\end{itemize}

\section*{Solution}
\begin{itemize}
\item[a)]
\[
\begin{aligned}
& b=\frac{2 \pi}{\frac{\pi}{4}} \\
& b=8 \\
& y=2 \sin (8 x)-3
\end{aligned}
\]
\item[1] mark for the value of \(b\)
\(\frac{1}{2}\) mark for amplitude
\(\frac{1}{2}\) mark for vertical translation
\end{itemize}

2 marks
